{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>By the sweat of your brow</b>: that he must labor to sow, grind, knead, and bake, unlike the food of beasts. And the meaning of בזעת is known from the words of the rabbis of blessed memory; it is on the pattern of שינה, and its root is יזע, like it: \"they shall not gird themselves with ביזע\" (Ezekiel 44:18), until they come to sweating. And since we know that man was created from the four elements, what is the meaning of \"for from it you were taken\"? The answer: the bones, their origin is from the dust, and therefore they are heavy and have no sensation, and they are the foundations of the body. Behold: \"and the bones came close, bone to its bone\" (Ezekiel 37:7), for they are like the form of a built house, and afterward: \"and behold, tendons were on them, and flesh came up, and skin covered them\" (ibid. 8). Likewise: \"and you shall carry up my bones\" (Genesis 50:25)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:18.310785524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}